.TH PAKMAN.PY 1 "2026-04-27" "1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
PakMan.py \- a robust Python package updater with per-package retries and logging
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 PakMan.py
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B PakMan.py
wraps
.B pip
to upgrade outdated Python packages with per-package retries, a failure
summary, optional freeze export, and a timestamped log at
.IR ~/.pakman.log .
.PP
Running without flags performs an interactive upgrade: it checks for outdated
packages, shows a table with current and latest versions, prompts for
confirmation, then upgrades each package individually — retrying failures before
reporting a summary.
.PP
All upgrades run per-package rather than in a single batch, so a failure in one
package does not abort the others.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Auto-approve all upgrades without an interactive prompt.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-only
List outdated packages with version info and exit without upgrading.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print every command that would be executed without running any of them.
Skips the confirmation prompt automatically.
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude " PKG " [ PKG " ...]"
Space-separated list of package names to skip. Matching is case-insensitive,
so
.B \-\-exclude pillow
matches
.BR Pillow .
.RS
.EX
python3 PakMan.py --exclude pip setuptools
.EE
.RE
.TP
.BI \-\-only " PKG " [ PKG " ...]"
Upgrade only the listed packages. Matching is case-insensitive. Packages not
in the outdated list are silently ignored. Specifying the same package in both
.B \-\-only
and
.B \-\-exclude
is an error.
.RS
.EX
python3 PakMan.py --only requests boto3
.EE
.RE
.TP
.B \-\-upgrade\-pip
Upgrade
.B pip
itself (via
.BR "pip install --upgrade pip" )
before upgrading any other packages.
.TP
.B \-\-pre
Pass
.B \-\-pre
to pip when upgrading, allowing installation of pre-release versions.
.TP
.BI \-\-export " FILE"
After all upgrades complete, run
.B pip freeze
and write the output to
.IR FILE .
If the freeze command fails, a warning is printed and the file is not written.
.RS
.EX
python3 PakMan.py -y --export requirements.txt
.EE
.RE
.TP
.B \-\-notify
Send a native macOS notification (via
.BR osascript )
when the run completes. Special characters in package names and error messages
are escaped to prevent AppleScript injection.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the outdated package list as a JSON array and exit. No upgrades are
performed. Each entry contains
.IR name ", " version ", " latest_version ", " latest_filetype .
.TP
.BI \-\-retries " N"
Number of retry attempts per package when an upgrade fails. Default is
.BR 2 .
Minimum value is
.BR 1 .
.SH FEATURES
.SS Per-Package Retries and Partial Failures
Each package is upgraded with its own
.B pip install --upgrade
call. On failure it retries up to
.B --retries N
times before being marked failed. All other packages continue regardless.
A summary is printed at the end:
.RS
.EX
\(bu some-package: error details here
.EE
.RE
.SS Outdated Table
Displays package name, installed version, latest available version, and
release type (wheel, sdist). Column widths are derived from the actual data,
so long package names are never truncated.
.SS Case-Insensitive Package Filtering
.B \-\-only
and
.B \-\-exclude
match package names case-insensitively against the canonical names returned
by pip. Specifying the same name in both flags is rejected at parse time.
.SS Virtualenv Warning
Detects whether a virtualenv is active. If not, prints a warning before
touching any global packages.
.SS pip Self-Upgrade
.B \-\-upgrade\-pip
runs
.B pip install --upgrade pip
before any other upgrades, ensuring the latest resolver is used.
.SS Freeze Export
.B \-\-export FILE
runs
.B pip freeze
after all upgrades and writes the output to
.IR FILE .
If the freeze command exits non-zero, a warning is printed and no file is
written.
.SS Upgrade Log
Every run appends timestamped entries to
.IR ~/.pakman.log
via Python's
.B logging
module:
.RS
.EX
[2026-03-28 14:05:01] --- PakMan run started ---
[2026-03-28 14:05:08] Upgraded: requests 2.28.0 -> 2.31.0
[2026-03-28 14:05:12] FAILED: some-pkg -- error details
[2026-03-28 14:05:13] Run complete with 1 failure(s). Elapsed: 12.4s
.EE
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Standard interactive upgrade:
.EX
python3 PakMan.py
.EE
.TP
Auto-approve, skip pip and setuptools, notify on completion:
.EX
python3 PakMan.py -y --exclude pip setuptools --notify
.EE
.TP
Preview outdated packages only:
.EX
python3 PakMan.py --check-only
.EE
.TP
Upgrade only specific packages:
.EX
python3 PakMan.py --only requests boto3 -y
.EE
.TP
Upgrade pip first, then everything, export freeze when done:
.EX
python3 PakMan.py --upgrade-pip -y --export requirements.txt
.EE
.TP
Include pre-release versions:
.EX
python3 PakMan.py --pre -y
.EE
.TP
Output outdated list as JSON for scripting:
.EX
python3 PakMan.py --json
.EE
.TP
Retry each failure up to 3 times:
.EX
python3 PakMan.py --retries 3 -y
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.pakman.log
Timestamped log of all PakMan runs, upgrades, and failures.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Python 3.10 or later.
.B pip
must be available for the active interpreter
.RB ( "python \-m pip" ).
.PP
The
.B \-\-notify
flag requires
.B osascript
(available by default on macOS).
.SH AUTHOR
Anirban Bagchi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pip (1),
.BR python3 (1)
